---
import BaseLayout from "../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Backup Space"
  description="Practical Oracle SQL for reviewing recovery area capacity, backup storage usage, archived redo volume and backup space trends."
>
  <main>
    <section class="resource-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">ORASOLU TOOLBOX · BACKUP &amp; RECOVERY</p>
        <h1>Backup <span class="hero-accent">Space</span></h1>
        <p>
          Practical Oracle SQL for reviewing recovery area capacity, backup storage
          usage, archived redo volume and backup space trends.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="resource-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="resource-intro">
          <p class="eyebrow">ORASOLU TOOLBOX · BACKUP &amp; RECOVERY</p>
          <h2>Measure backup space before it becomes a recovery problem</h2>
          <p>
            Backup investigations should show how much recovery area is configured,
            which file types consume space, how large RMAN backups are and how
            archived redo contributes to storage growth. These queries provide a
            practical starting point for reviewing backup space.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-grid">
          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <p class="resource-block__label">01 · RECOVERY AREA</p>
              <h2>Review recovery area capacity</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Review configured recovery area space, current usage, reclaimable
              space and the number of files stored in the destination.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    name,
    space_limit / 1024 / 1024 / 1024 AS limit_gb,
    space_used / 1024 / 1024 / 1024 AS used_gb,
    space_reclaimable / 1024 / 1024 / 1024 AS reclaimable_gb,
    number_of_files
FROM v$recovery_file_dest;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <p class="resource-block__label">02 · SPACE BY TYPE</p>
              <h2>Find recovery area space consumers</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Break down recovery area usage by file type to identify where the
              available space is being consumed.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    file_type,
    percent_space_used,
    percent_space_reclaimable,
    number_of_files
FROM v$recovery_area_usage
ORDER BY percent_space_used DESC;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <p class="resource-block__label">03 · BACKUP PIECES</p>
              <h2>Review RMAN backup piece space</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Review RMAN backup piece sizes and completion times to identify
              large backup files and recent storage consumption.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    completion_time,
    handle,
    bytes / 1024 / 1024 / 1024 AS size_gb,
    status
FROM v$backup_piece
WHERE deleted = 'NO'
ORDER BY completion_time DESC;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <p class="resource-block__label">04 · BACKUP SETS</p>
              <h2>Measure backup set size</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Review backup set sizes by completion time to understand how much
              storage individual RMAN backup sets require.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    completion_time,
    backup_type,
    incremental_level,
    backup_size / 1024 / 1024 / 1024 AS size_gb
FROM v$backup_set
ORDER BY completion_time DESC;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <p class="resource-block__label">05 · ARCHIVED REDO</p>
              <h2>Measure archived redo volume</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Summarize archived redo volume by day to identify periods of high
              redo generation that can increase backup storage requirements.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    TRUNC(completion_time) AS archive_day,
    ROUND(
        SUM(blocks * block_size) / 1024 / 1024 / 1024,
        2
    ) AS archived_redo_gb
FROM v$archived_log
WHERE completion_time IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY TRUNC(completion_time)
ORDER BY archive_day DESC;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <p class="resource-block__label">06 · DAILY BACKUP GROWTH</p>
              <h2>Track recent backup growth</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Summarize recent RMAN backup piece volume by day to identify
              changes in backup storage requirements.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    TRUNC(completion_time) AS backup_day,
    ROUND(
        SUM(bytes) / 1024 / 1024 / 1024,
        2
    ) AS backup_gb
FROM v$backup_piece
WHERE deleted = 'NO'
  AND status = 'A'
  AND completion_time &gt;= SYSDATE - 30
GROUP BY TRUNC(completion_time)
ORDER BY backup_day DESC;</code></pre>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-note">
          <p class="eyebrow">ORASOLU TOOLBOX · BACKUP &amp; RECOVERY</p>
          <h2>Backup space should be measured as a storage lifecycle.</h2>
          <p>
            Recovery area capacity, RMAN backup pieces, backup sets and archived
            redo all contribute to the storage picture. Reviewing them together
            helps identify growth patterns before space pressure affects backup
            or recovery operations.
          </p>
          <p>
            These queries use Oracle dynamic performance views including
            <code>V$RECOVERY_FILE_DEST</code>,
            <code>V$RECOVERY_AREA_USAGE</code>,
            <code>V$BACKUP_PIECE</code>,
            <code>V$BACKUP_SET</code> and
            <code>V$ARCHIVED_LOG</code>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-actions">
          <a class="button button--primary" href="/tools/backup-recovery/">
            Back to Backup &amp; Recovery
          </a>
          <a class="resource-actions__link" href="/tools/backup-recovery/recovery-diagnostics/">
            Read Recovery Diagnostics
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.resource-hero {
  padding-top: 82px;
  padding-bottom: 72px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
}
.resource-hero h1 {
  margin: 0 0 14px;
  color: var(--ink);
  font-size: clamp(42px, 6vw, 72px);
  line-height: 1.05;
  letter-spacing: -0.04em;
}
.resource-hero .hero-accent {
  color: var(--orange);
}
.resource-hero > .container > p:last-child {
  max-width: 900px;
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 17px;
  line-height: 1.75;
}
.resource-section {
  padding-top: 56px;
  padding-bottom: 72px;
}
.resource-intro {
  max-width: 820px;
  margin-bottom: 32px;
}
.resource-intro .eyebrow {
  margin: 0 0 14px;
  color: var(--orange);
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  line-height: 1.2;
}
.resource-intro h2 {
  margin: 0 0 14px;
  color: var(--ink);
  font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 38px);
  line-height: 1.15;
}
.resource-intro p:not(.eyebrow) {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 16px;
  line-height: 1.75;
}
.resource-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: 22px;
  align-items: start;
}
.resource-block {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  min-width: 0;
  height: 560px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  overflow: hidden;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 30px;
  background: #ffffff;
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: 18px;
  transition:
    border-color 0.22s ease,
    box-shadow 0.22s ease,
    transform 0.22s ease;
}
.resource-block:hover {
  border-color: #d8dce1;
  box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(17, 29, 44, 0.06);
  transform: translateY(-3px);
}
.resource-block__header {
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}
.resource-block__label {
  margin-bottom: 9px;
  color: var(--orange);
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  line-height: 1.2;
}
.resource-block h2 {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--ink);
  font-size: 22px;
  line-height: 1.3;
}
.resource-block__description {
  min-height: 48px;
  margin: 0 0 22px;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 14px;
  line-height: 1.7;
}
.resource-block pre {
  position: relative;
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  min-height: 0;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 22px;
  overflow-x: auto;
  overflow-y: auto;
  white-space: pre;
  background: #2f353d;
  border-radius: 10px;
  color: #f3f4f6;
  font-family:
    "Cascadia Code",
    "Consolas",
    "Courier New",
    monospace;
  font-size: 13px;
  line-height: 1.7;
}
.resource-block code {
  font-family: inherit;
  white-space: pre;
}
.resource-copy-button {
  position: absolute;
  top: 10px;
  right: 10px;
  padding: 5px 9px;
  border: 1px solid #d1d5db;
  border-radius: 5px;
  background: #ffffff;
  color: #374151;
  font-family: inherit;
  font-size: 0.75rem;
  cursor: pointer;
  z-index: 2;
}
.resource-copy-button:hover {
  background: #f3f4f6;
}
.resource-note {
  max-width: 820px;
  margin-top: 56px;
  padding: 30px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  background: #f7f8fa;
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: 18px;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 14px;
  line-height: 1.75;
}
.resource-note .eyebrow {
  margin: 0 0 14px;
}
.resource-note h2 {
  margin: 0 0 14px;
  color: var(--ink);
  font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 38px);
  line-height: 1.15;
}
.resource-note p:not(.eyebrow) {
  margin: 0 0 14px;
}
.resource-note p:last-child {
  margin-bottom: 0;
}
.resource-note code {
  padding: 1px 4px;
  border-radius: 4px;
  background: #eef0f2;
  color: var(--ink);
  font-family:
    "Cascadia Code",
    "Consolas",
    "Courier New",
    monospace;
  font-size: 0.92em;
}
.resource-actions {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 24px;
  justify-content: flex-start;
  margin-top: 32px;
}
.resource-actions__link {
  color: var(--orange);
  font-size: 14px;
  font-weight: 700;
  text-decoration: none;
}
.resource-actions__link:hover {
  text-decoration: underline;
}
@media (max-width: 820px) {
  .resource-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}
@media (max-width: 680px) {
  .resource-hero {
    padding-top: 58px;
    padding-bottom: 54px;
  }
  .resource-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(38px, 12vw, 54px);
  }
  .resource-section {
    padding-top: 42px;
    padding-bottom: 56px;
  }
  .resource-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .resource-block {
    height: 520px;
    padding: 22px;
    border-radius: 16px;
  }
  .resource-block__description {
    min-height: 0;
  }
  .resource-block pre {
    padding: 18px;
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .resource-note {
    padding: 22px;
    border-radius: 16px;
  }
  .resource-actions {
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 16px;
  }
}
</style>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll(".resource-block pre").forEach((pre) => {
    const button = document.createElement("button");
    button.type = "button";
    button.className = "resource-copy-button";
    button.textContent = "Copy";
    button.setAttribute("aria-label", "Copy SQL");

    pre.style.position = "relative";
    button.style.position = "absolute";
    button.style.top = "10px";
    button.style.right = "10px";
    button.style.padding = "5px 9px";
    button.style.border = "1px solid #d1d5db";
    button.style.borderRadius = "5px";
    button.style.background = "#ffffff";
    button.style.color = "#374151";
    button.style.fontFamily = "inherit";
    button.style.fontSize = "0.75rem";
    button.style.cursor = "pointer";
    button.style.zIndex = "2";

    button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const code = pre.querySelector("code");
      if (!code) return;

      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(code.textContent || "");
        button.textContent = "Copied";
        window.setTimeout(() => {
          button.textContent = "Copy";
        }, 1500);
      } catch {
        button.textContent = "Copy failed";
        window.setTimeout(() => {
          button.textContent = "Copy";
        }, 1500);
      }
    });

    pre.appendChild(button);
  });
</script>
